questions.stem:
A bakery schedules a shift code as a Java int literal written in octal. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Bakery {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int shift = 010;
        System.out.println(shift);
    }
}

A bakery developer writes a tray-count literal that the compiler refuses. Trace what happens to this program.

class Bakery {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int trays = 018;
        System.out.println(trays);
    }
}

A transit system counts loaded carriages with a hexadecimal int literal. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Transit {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int cartons = 0x1F;
        System.out.println(cartons);
    }
}

A transit route number is written as a hexadecimal int literal using an upper-case prefix and lower-case digits. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Transit {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int route = 0XaB;
        System.out.println(route);
    }
}

A robotics club stores a bit mask for four sensors as a binary int literal. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Robotics {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int mask = 0b1010;
        System.out.println(mask);
    }
}

A bakery developer writes a large hexadecimal constant in a long variable and the compiler refuses it. Trace what happens to this program.

class Bakery {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        long total = 0xFFFFFFFFF;
        System.out.println(total);
    }
}

A transit system writes an all-ones mask in hexadecimal with separators for readability. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Transit {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int mask = 0xFF_FF;
        System.out.println(mask);
    }
}

A bakery splits a payroll total by the number of bakeries sharing it. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Bakery {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        long payroll = 1_000L;
        System.out.println(payroll / 500);
    }
}

A robotics club records an arm span in millimetres using a scientific-notation double. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Robotics {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double span = 1.5e3;
        System.out.println(span);
    }
}

A robotics club writes a reach distance using a scientific literal whose mantissa has no decimal point. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Robotics {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double reach = 1e3;
        System.out.println(reach);
    }
}

A robotics club stores a servo travel limit as a single-precision scientific literal. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Robotics {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        float reach = 1.5e2f;
        System.out.println(reach);
    }
}

A robotics club measures a long detection range and lets the program print the double directly. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Robotics {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double far = 1.5e10;
        System.out.println(far);
    }
}

A bakery seats a large catering order and adds two seat counts into a long. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Bakery {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int seats = 2000000000;
        long total = seats + seats;
        System.out.println(total);
    }
}

A bakery seats a large catering order and adds an int seat count to a long figure that needs no wrapping. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Bakery {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int seats = 2000000000;
        long total = seats + 1000000000L;
        System.out.println(total);
    }
}

A pharmacy keeps a running long count and adds one past the largest long. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Pharmacy {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        long doses = Long.MAX_VALUE + 1;
        System.out.println(doses);
    }
}

A pharmacy converts a storage temperature that hit the coldest int reading into a positive offset. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Pharmacy {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int coldest = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int flipped = -coldest;
        System.out.println(flipped);
    }
}

A bakery labels aisles with letters and shifts an aisle letter forward by one inside an expression. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Bakery {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char aisle = 'A';
        System.out.println(aisle + 1);
    }
}

A bakery advances an aisle letter with a compound assignment and then prints the letter and its code unit. Trace the program and give both lines it prints.

class Bakery {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char aisle = 'A';
        aisle += 1;
        System.out.println(aisle);
        System.out.println(aisle + 1);
    }
}

A bakery developer tries to shift an aisle letter with a plain assignment and the compiler refuses it. Trace what happens to this program.

class Bakery {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char aisle = 'A';
        aisle = aisle + 1;
        System.out.println(aisle);
    }
}

A bakery stores a whole tray count in a double so later maths can use fractions. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Bakery {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int trays = 8;
        double shown = trays;
        System.out.println(shown);
    }
}

A pharmacy needs a whole number of kilograms and casts a measured weight down to an int. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Pharmacy {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double kg = 9.99;
        int whole = (int) kg;
        System.out.println(whole);
    }
}

A transit system converts a sub-zero platform reading down to a whole number by casting. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Transit {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double temp = -9.99;
        int whole = (int) temp;
        System.out.println(whole);
    }
}

A transit sensor reports a distance so large that it cannot fit in an int, and the code casts it anyway. Trace the program and give the line it prints.

class Transit {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double huge = 1.0e20;
        int capped = (int) huge;
        System.out.println(capped);
    }
}

A transit billing routine reads an octal shift count and a hexadecimal route number, adds a route charge to a large long subtotal, and then prints the shift. Trace the program and give both lines it prints.

class Transit {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int route = 0x1F;
        int shift = 010;
        long total = 2_000_000_000L + route * 1000;
        System.out.println(total);
        System.out.println(shift);
    }
}
